window.GLOSS={};
window.EN={"1":"The fierce battle at the royal capital, Belhalla, claimed the lives of most of the powerful nobles,","2":"and Lord Arvis, exactly as he had planned, seized total control of the kingdom.","3":"He destroyed the two rival kingdoms of Silesse and Leonster, unifying the continent,","4":"and with the overwhelming support of the people","5":"he became the first emperor of the Grannvale Empire.","6":"Seventeen years passed since the battle of Belhalla.","7":"The people who once hailed Emperor Arvis with such enthusiasm","8":"now groaned and suffered under his tyranny,","9":"and in the outlying nations under the Empire's rule,","10":"people were forced to live like slaves.","11":"Here in Isaac too, the people's suffering had reached its limit.","12":"King Danan of Isaac, like his father Duke Langobalt,","13":"was a cruel man.","14":"He reduced the people of Isaac to slavery,","15":"and while he himself indulged in pleasure at the palace in Ribot,","16":"he placed his second son Johan at Isaac Castle, his third son Johalva at Sophara Castle,","17":"and at the remote Ganeishire Castle he placed his trusted General Harold,","18":"ruling the people with a heavy hand.","19":"But the people of Isaac still had hope.","20":"In the hidden village of Tirnanog to the north, Prince Shanan's Liberation Army had formed,","21":"and day by day it grew stronger.","22":"And among those young warriors was a boy the people of Isaac called the Prince of Light,","23":"and revered as the prince of Grannvale.","24":"The young leader of the Liberation Army; his name was Celice.","25":"(Danan): Harold, how goes the search for the rebels?","26":"(Danan): How much longer do you intend to let them run wild!","27":"(Danan): Prince Shanan's rebel army grows bigger every year, and gets in our way at every turn.","28":"(Danan): And on top of that, I hear they're even harboring the child of that traitor Sigurd.","29":"(Danan): This leaves me, as King of Isaac, with no standing at all.","30":"(Danan): What am I to say to His Majesty the Emperor to apologize for this!","31":"(Papillon): Hah, my deepest apologies, Lord Danan. But please be at ease.","32":"(Papillon): We've already located the rebels' hideout, and a punitive force has already been sent out.","33":"(Papillon): They're nothing more than rats in a sack now. We'll strike down every last one.","34":"(Danan): Hmph, is that so... But let me say this: do not grow careless.","35":"(Danan): The brats are fine, but the real problem is Oifey and Shanan.","36":"(Danan): Underestimate those two alone, and you'll pay dearly for it.","37":"(Papillon): Yes, I'm well aware. But as it happens, from what we've quietly looked into,","38":"(Papillon): neither Oifey nor Shanan is at the Tirnanog hideout. It seems they're both out.","39":"(Danan): What? Is that true! Then don't dawdle. Give the order to attack at once!","40":"(Danan): The people of Isaac call them the Liberation Army and treat them like heroes.","41":"(Danan): There's no need for mercy — this will serve as an example. Kill them! Kill them all!!","42":"(Danan): I'll be heading back to Ribot. I expect good news waiting for me.","43":"(Scathach): Lord Celice, this is terrible! It seems the enemy has found this hideout!","44":"(Scathach): Word has come that a punitive force has set out from Ganeishire!!","45":"(Lakche): Scathach, what are you panicking for? We always knew this hideout would be found eventually.","46":"(Lakche): If they're coming to us, that just saves us the trouble.","47":"(Lakche): Let's meet them head on, and while we're at it, push on to Ganeishire.","48":"(Scathach): Lakche, don't talk nonsense.","49":"(Scathach): Prince Shanan has gone off to the Temple of Yied, and Oifey and the others still aren't back either.","50":"(Scathach): How are we supposed to fight with just the two of us?","51":"(Lakche): Oh my, is Scathach scared? I'm not worried at all. Besides, isn't this a chance?","52":"(Lakche): The prince always treated us like children and wouldn't let us into real battle, but I've trained more than enough by now.","53":"(Scathach): But, Lakche...","54":"(Lakche): I... I don't want to keep running away anymore. They're beasts! So many of my friends have been killed.","55":"(Lakche): Imperial soldiers chasing down girls who try to flee, one after another...","56":"(Lakche): Back then, if Prince Shanan hadn't come to save me, I'd be dead too.","57":"(Lakche): ...I will never forget those girls' sorrow!","58":"(Scathach): Lakche... I know how frustrated you are... but still...","59":"(Celice): Scathach is worried about me.","60":"(Celice): He was probably told sternly by Shanan to hold back.","61":"(Celice): Otherwise he'd be the first one charging out there.","62":"(Celice): Scathach is dying to fight too.","63":"(Lakche): Ah, ...that's... true, I suppose... Indeed, we can't go dragging Lord Celice into this too...","64":"(Celice): What, Lakche, you too? I'm not a child anymore either. I can fight alongside all of you.","65":"(Celice): And besides, this Tirnanog is a precious home to me,","66":"(Celice): I can't just abandon the people who took care of me and run.","67":"(Scathach): But even so...","68":"(Celice): There's no time to waste — Lana, I'm counting on you to look after the townspeople. We'll go meet the enemy at the western hollow.","69":"(Nanna): Lord Celice, I'm coming too!","70":"(Celice): No, you're a sister, you're not suited for battle.","71":"(Nanna): Even a sister can fight! I feel the same way as Lakche,","72":"(Nanna): the Empire's soldiers grow crueler by the day,","73":"(Nanna): and women and children especially can't go on living like this. I don't want us to be destroyed like this.","74":"(Nanna): I have my own way of fighting!","75":"(Celice): I see... I'm sorry, Nanna. You're right. This is everyone's fight.","76":"(Celice): Alright, let's go together. I don't know how it'll turn out, but","77":"(Celice): let's do everything we can right now.","78":"(Nanna): Yes, Lord Celice! But... I'm sorry for speaking out of turn.","79":"(Celice): Hahaha... it's fine. Now then, Scathach, Lakche, Nanna, let's go!","80":"(Oifey): Damn it... I'm too late, the battle's already begun.","81":"(Lester): While we were going around checking on the other countries' conditions, it seems word of Tirnanog got out.","82":"(Lester): I hope everyone's alright.","83":"(Delmud): Lester, don't talk about it like it's none of your concern.","84":"(Delmud): Your sister Nanna might be caught up in the fighting too, you know.","85":"(Delmud): Lord Oifey, let's hurry — I'm worried about Lord Celice!","86":"(Oifey): You're right, Delmud, Lester — let's race to the battlefield at full speed!","87":"(Scathach): Lakche, are you alright?","88":"(Lakche): Yeah, somehow or other...","89":"(Scathach): Don't push yourself too hard. You're always so reckless.","90":"(Lakche): I know that already. I'm not a child anymore.","91":"(Scathach): Prince Shanan said your fiery temper is just like your mother's.","92":"(Lakche): You mean Mother Ayra... but I don't remember her at all. What about you, Scathach?","93":"(Scathach): I don't remember her either.","94":"(Scathach): After all, you and I are twins, and we hadn't even turned two yet.","95":"(Scathach): Oifey brought us to safety in Isaac, but Mother never came back.","96":"(Scathach): I suppose she must have died in the battle of Belhalla after all...","97":"(Lakche): Scathach! You promised never to say that! Mother is alive!!","98":"(Lakche): Don't ever say such a thing again!","99":"(Scathach): ...I'm sorry, Lakche... you're right... sorry.","100":"(Rodolvan): Radney, are you alright?","101":"(Radney): Yeah, somehow or other...","102":"(Rodolvan): Don't push yourself too hard. You're always so reckless.","103":"(Radney): I know that already. I'm not a child anymore.","104":"(Rodolvan): But it's strange, isn't it. I can't understand what Johan or Johalva are thinking.","105":"(Radney): I find it so troublesome. I hate men! It makes my skin crawl.","106":"(Rodolvan): Your hatred of men is because of those imperial soldiers, isn't it. But not all men are like that.","107":"(Radney): Yes, I know that. But I still can't accept it... just being near them makes me feel sick.","108":"(Rodolvan): Any man at all?","109":"(Radney): Of course Lord Celice and Rodolvan are different.","110":"(Rodolvan): Heh, and Lord Shanan too, I suppose.","111":"(Radney): Ro-, Rodolvan!!","112":"(Oifey): Lord Celice, I'm glad to see you safe!","113":"(Celice): Oifey, you've come back. How were things in the other countries?","114":"(Oifey): Yes, the situation is only getting worse. People all over the world are groaning under the Empire's tyranny, and uprisings are breaking out everywhere.","115":"(Celice): I thought as much... so it's not only Isaac suffering under the Empire's tyranny.","116":"(Celice): Oifey, isn't there any way we could save them?","117":"(Oifey): I'm afraid that right now we don't have anywhere near enough strength to fight the Empire.","118":"(Celice): But Isaac's war of liberation has already begun. There's no turning back now...","119":"(Oifey): Yes, now that Lord Celice's whereabouts are known, we can no longer stay hidden.","120":"(Oifey): It's a rather reckless fight, but it seems there's no helping it now...","121":"(Celice): I feel bad for starting this fight on my own.","122":"(Celice): But the people of Isaac can't endure Danan's tyranny any longer. Oifey, please understand...","123":"(Oifey): Yes, Lord Celice. In that case, we should press on to the capital, Ribot, as soon as possible.","124":"(Oifey): If we dawdle, the Empire's reinforcements might arrive!","125":"(Lester): Nanna!? You've joined the fighting too?","126":"(Nanna): Yes, brother Lester. Because I was worried about Lord Celice...","127":"(Lester): I see, I thought as much...","128":"(Lester): But please be careful. If anything happened to you, Mother would be heartbroken.","129":"(Nanna): Yes, but you know, brother, Mother Ethlyn told us","130":"(Nanna): that since we owe the people of Isaac so much, we should do whatever we can for them.","131":"(Lester): Yes, if this country's people hadn't helped us, we wouldn't have survived.","132":"(Lester): ...so, how is Mother?","133":"(Nanna): She's working at the convent in Tirnanog.","134":"(Lester): I see... Nanna, for Mother's sake, and for the sake of the father we've never met, let's do our best.","135":"(Lester): And someday, surely, we'll return to Mother's homeland, Jungby.","136":"(Nanna): Yes, brother Lester.","137":"(Dimna): Mana!? You've joined the fighting too?","138":"(Mana): That's right, brother Dimna. Because I'm worried about Lord Celice.","139":"(Dimna): Hmph, I thought as much...","140":"(Mana): Wh-, what do you mean...","141":"(Dimna): Well... fine, I suppose, but don't get in over your head.","142":"(Dimna): Lord Celice carries the noble blood of the Grannvale royal family.","143":"(Dimna): Commoners like us really shouldn't even be allowed near him — it'll be you who ends up crying over it.","144":"(Mana): That's not... brother, you've got it all wrong.","145":"(Mana): I just want to protect Lord Celice, that's all.","146":"(Dimna): Is that so... then that's fine. Sorry, Mana, I just worry about you, that's all...","147":"(Mana): Yeah, I know... thank you, brother Dimna...","148":"(Soldier): Lord Johalva really has strange tastes, doesn't he. What does he see in such a hot-tempered woman anyway.","149":"(Soldier): If it were me, I'd rather— Wha, what are you trying to make me say!? ......","150":"(Soldier): Hah, Lord Johan's a handful too. He's completely weak when it comes to women, but brutally strict with us.","151":"(Johan): Did you say something?","152":"(Soldier): N-, no! It was nothing at all, sir! Yessir!","153":"(Papillon): Damn it... mere rebels, of all things!","154":"(Papillon): Guh, ...why... ...how could I lose to such a ragtag band of soldiers...!?","155":"(Celice): So this is Ganeishire... it's been thoroughly ravaged...","156":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, it's been a while.","157":"(Celice): Huh? ...oh, ...Levin!! ...no, ...King Levin of Silesse...","158":"(Levin (Strategist)): Just call me Levin, like the old days. After the battle of Belhalla, Silesse was occupied by the Empire.","159":"(Levin (Strategist)): I'm still disgracing myself by living on like this, but","160":"(Levin (Strategist)): Silesse itself perished with its pride intact, together with my mother.","161":"(Levin (Strategist)): Now as before, I'm nothing but a foolish wandering minstrel. I don't know what Oifey might have told you, but whatever you do, don't call me a king.","162":"(Celice): Levin... I'm sorry...","163":"(Levin (Strategist)): Hahaha, that was just a joke, don't worry about it. More importantly, so it's finally begun. It was worth the long wait.","164":"(Levin (Strategist)): There's no country better suited for raising an army against the Empire than Isaac.","165":"(Celice): Yes, the people of this country have courage, and they hate the Empire with all their hearts.","166":"(Celice): Though honestly, things would be much easier if Prince Shanan were here.","167":"(Levin (Strategist)): Did Shanan go to the Temple of Yied?","168":"(Celice): Yes, there was information that the Isaac royal family's treasure, the holy sword Balmung, is at the Temple of Yied...","169":"(Celice): But apparently that place is ruled by a wicked dark priest, and everyone's worried about him.","170":"(Levin (Strategist)): Well, knowing him, there's no need to worry. More importantly, Celice, I have a favor to ask.","171":"(Celice): Oh? What is it? If it's something I can do, I'd be glad to help.","172":"(Levin (Strategist)): Julia, come here. This child — I rescued her as a small girl, collapsed in the capital of Belhalla,","173":"(Levin (Strategist)): and I've been keeping her hidden on the frontier of Silesse until now,","174":"(Levin (Strategist)): but even that place has finally become dangerous, so I had no choice but to bring her along.","175":"(Levin (Strategist)): But I have to go on to Leonster from here, and she'd be a bit of a burden.","176":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, I'm sorry to ask, but could you look after her for a while?","177":"(Levin (Strategist)): This girl has had a hard life. She seems to have suffered some terrible shock,","178":"(Levin (Strategist)): because when I rescued her, she didn't have a single memory left. Even now, she still doesn't...","179":"(Celice): ! ...I had no idea... understood, leave her to me.","180":"(Celice): But please come back for her as soon as you can. Julia must be feeling anxious too...","181":"(Levin (Strategist)): Ah, I know. By the time you've taken all of Isaac, I'll be back too.","182":"(Levin (Strategist)): Well then, good luck, Celice.","183":"(Celice): Take care too, Levin!","184":"(Celice): Julia, I know it must be unsettling, but there's nothing to worry about.","185":"(Celice): Until Levin comes back, I'll protect you... though, honestly,","186":"(Celice): I'm not really all that strong yet.","187":"(Celice): But I'll do my best to grow stronger, strong enough to protect everyone,","188":"(Celice): and to save everyone from the Empire's tyranny — I'll become strong, just like my father...","189":"(Julia): Lord Celice.........","190":"(Danan): Ganeishire has fallen into the rebels' hands, you say? Harold, you fool!","191":"(Danan): What are my sons doing! Tell them to crush the rebels at once!","192":"(Johalva): Father's giving an attack order, huh? Fight the army with Lakche in it? Damn it, what am I supposed to do...","193":"(Johan): Attack Ganeishire, is it? Good grief, father's orders...","194":"(Johan): But... I could never fight Lakche. Ahh, what on earth should I do...","195":"(Fee): Whew, sorry, Mana. Was I heavy?","196":"(Arthur): Hmm, so that pegasus is called Mana.","197":"(Fee): Arthur, would you quit it already! \"Just a little further, just a little further\" you kept saying, and we ended up all the way out here in Isaac!","198":"(Arthur): Sorry for the imposition, Fee. Just a bit further — well, never mind, I'll walk the rest of the way.","199":"(Fee): Where on earth are you even trying to go?","200":"(Arthur): Alster.","201":"(Fee): Al-, Alster!? Are you out of your mind.","202":"(Fee): Alster, if I remember right, is way to the south, across the sea,","203":"(Fee): do you have any idea how far that is from here... there's no way you can walk it!","204":"(Arthur): It's fine, it's not like I'm in any particular hurry.","205":"(Fee): So what's even in Alster?","206":"(Arthur): There's a little sister there, apparently, who I was separated from when we were small.","207":"(Arthur): When I was little, my mother and sister were taken from me, and I grew up all alone in some corner of Silesse,","208":"(Arthur): but hearing a story like that, well, I just... I want to see her...","209":"(Fee): Huh, is that so. I understand, that feeling. I want to see my brother too, you know.","210":"(Arthur): You were separated too?","211":"(Fee): No, we were together in Silesse the whole time. But my brother left on a journey, saying he was going to look for our father.","212":"(Arthur): Your father?","213":"(Fee): Our father, you see, has gone missing. Mother waited and waited, but he never came back.","214":"(Arthur): And what happened to your mother?","215":"(Fee): She died, of illness...","216":"(Arthur): I see... sorry, that was a strange thing to ask.","217":"(Fee): It's fine. I used to think you were a strange one, but you're not such a bad person after all.","218":"(Arthur): Hahaha, well, thank you very much. So you've reconsidered your opinion of me, have you.","219":"(Fee): I suppose so. So, what are you really going to do from here?","220":"(Arthur): Hmm, well, I don't know... but what about you?","221":"(Fee): I'm going to join Isaac's Liberation Army.","222":"(Fee): When I was little, my mother told me the story of the holy knight Sigurd and the brave warriors — I always admired it.","223":"(Fee): And now that very Sigurd's own son has risen up here in Isaac.","224":"(Fee): I figured I'd better do my part too, so I rushed out of Silesse in a hurry.","225":"(Arthur): Heh, sounds interesting. Alright, I'll lend a hand for a while too — I owe you for the ride, after all.","226":"(Fee): Okay, now you're talking! Let's do our best, partner!","227":"(Arthur): Hahaha, you're a lively one.","228":"(Danan): What are they doing! Those useless sons of mine, don't they even know how to fight!","229":"(Danan): Schmidt, you go — take back the castle the rebels stole from us!","230":"(Slayder): Yes, Lord Danan, leave it to me.","231":"(Nanna): Hello, Julia. You must be lonely without Lord Levin around.","232":"(Julia): You're Nanna, aren't you. No, I'm fine. I'm not lonely at all.","233":"(Nanna): Lord Celice has been very worried about you, you know.","234":"(Nanna): If anything's troubling you, just tell me.","235":"(Julia): Alright, thank you...","236":"(Nanna): And here, this is for you.","237":"(Julia): Is this a Revive staff?","238":"(Nanna): Yes, I'm sure you can use it, can't you?","239":"(Julia): You're giving this to me? ...thank you, Nanna.","240":"(Julia): Now I can be of use to everyone too.","241":"(Nanna): Julia, let's work hard together, and do our best!","242":"(Johan): Ah, Lakche... my beloved... the day of destiny has finally come...","243":"(Lakche): Johan? What are you talking about? Did you eat something bad?","244":"(Johan): Lakche... your words are a little bird's song, your eyes are the twinkling of the stars.","245":"(Johan): Ah, I can no longer live without you any longer...","246":"(Lakche): Stop it, it's disgusting! This is a battlefield, you know — you can't possibly be in your right mind.","247":"(Johan): I'll show you proof that my heart speaks no falsehood. Love can drive a man mad, at times.","248":"(Johan): Hear me, all my troops — from this moment, our army sides with the Liberation Army!","249":"(Johan): From today, we fight for love, for justice, and for Lakche!!","250":"(Johalva): Damn it, brother Johan! Sneaking off ahead of me and siding with Lakche.","251":"(Johalva): Fine then, I'll fight! All troops, to the attack!","252":"(Johalva): Well if it isn't Lakche! Did you come all this way just because you wanted to see me?","253":"(Lakche): Heh, Johalva... same as ever, I see. You may be rough around the edges, but you really aren't a bad person.","254":"(Lakche): At the very least, you never laid a hand on women or children.","255":"(Lakche): If I could help it, I wouldn't want to fight either, you know.","256":"(Johalva): I'm not cool and composed like my brothers, you know. I'm not the type to force things through with brute strength.","257":"(Johalva): And besides, I can't stand the Loptr cult's ways anymore.","258":"(Johalva): I hear they're sacrificing innocent children back home,","259":"(Johalva): and I'm sick and tired of my old man too, who can't even say a word against it.","260":"(Johalva): If Lakche wants it, I'll hand my whole unit over to you.","261":"(Lakche): Wha! ...are you serious? Johalva, you really are something...","262":"(Lakche): I'm sorry, it seems I've misjudged you a little, all this time.","263":"(Johalva): It's fine. I really have done some awful things, so call this making up for it, I'll do it.","264":"(Johalva): Alright then, from today we're the Liberation Army! You lot, fight for love and justice!!","265":"(Johan): Johalva has sided with the Liberation Army, you say? Damn... Johalva, sneaking ahead of me like that!","266":"(Johan): Fine then, all troops, begin the attack!","267":"(Arthur): Lord Celice, nice to meet you.","268":"(Celice): You are...?","269":"(Arthur): I'm Arthur. I've come from Silesse.","270":"(Celice): So you're Arthur!? I hear you helped everyone out — thank you.","271":"(Arthur): No, don't mention it.","272":"(Celice): So you can use magic? That's impressive.","273":"(Arthur): My mother was a mage knight, so... but I'm still nowhere near good enough.","274":"(Celice): That's the same for all of us.","275":"(Celice): But if we all join our strength together, we might be able to change the world. That's the thought that made us rise up.","276":"(Arthur): I see... for whatever little I can do, I'll lend my strength too. Lord Celice, I look forward to working with you.","277":"(Fee): Are you Lord Celice!","278":"(Celice): Yes, that's right, and you are?","279":"(Fee): I've come from Silesse. My name's Fee.","280":"(Celice): Silesse? Are you a pegasus knight?","281":"(Fee): No, not yet, but... my mother was a pegasus knight.","282":"(Fee): In the last war, she fought alongside Lord Sigurd.","283":"(Celice): I see... on my father's behalf, let me thank you. But why have you come?","284":"(Fee): The truth is I set out from home to look for my brother,","285":"(Fee): but when I heard Lord Celice had begun a fight to overthrow the Empire, I just couldn't stay away any longer...","286":"(Fee): Lord Celice, please let me join the Liberation Army too.","287":"(Celice): I don't mind that, but is it alright with your brother?","288":"(Fee): Yes, I think that if I stay with Lord Celice's army, I'll be able to meet my brother too. I just have that feeling...","289":"(Femina): Are you Lord Celice!","290":"(Celice): Yes, that's right, and you are?","291":"(Femina): I've come from Silesse. My name's Femina.","292":"(Celice): Silesse? Are you a pegasus knight?","293":"(Femina): Yes, though I'm still only in training...","294":"(Celice): I see... but why have you come to Isaac?","295":"(Femina): The truth is I set out from home to look for my brother,","296":"(Femina): but when I heard Lord Celice had begun a fight to overthrow the Empire, I just couldn't stay away any longer...","297":"(Femina): Lord Celice, please let me join the Liberation Army too.","298":"(Celice): I don't mind that, but is it alright with your brother?","299":"(Femina): Yes, I think that if I stay with Lord Celice's army, I'll be able to meet my brother too. I just have that feeling...","300":"(Lakche): Hey! Quit hovering around me! It's annoying!","301":"(Johan): Now now, don't be so cold. This is simply how I express my love.","302":"(Johan): Please don't forget that I'm always watching over you.","303":"(Lakche): .........","304":"(Lakche): Hey! Quit hovering around me! It's annoying!","305":"(Johalva): Ugh..., I just... thought I'd protect you...","306":"(Lakche): .........","307":"(Johan): Heheheh... there's no one who can beat me.","308":"(Johan): Rejoice, that you get to die at my hand.","309":"(Johan): Ahh, to lose to mere rebels... Lakche, my love is eternal...","310":"(Johalva): I'm not handing my castle over to you! You rebels, I'll beat you senseless!","311":"(Johalva): Ugh... Lakche... ...I'm sorry...","312":"(Elder): Lord Celice, thank you for liberating this town.","313":"(Celice): Elder, is everyone in the town safe?","314":"(Elder): Yes, we're all overjoyed.","315":"(Celice): Please bear with it just a little longer — I will defeat King Danan of Ribot without fail, and liberate all of Isaac.","316":"(Elder): What encouraging words. But please, do not push yourself too hard.","317":"(Elder): Lord Celice, you are now the only hope for the people of this world.","318":"(Elder): For it is you, and you alone, who can save this dark world...","319":"(Elder): Well, well, Lord Celice, I'm so glad you're safe.","320":"(Celice): Elder, is everyone in the town safe?","321":"(Elder): Yes, we're all overjoyed. Thanks to Lord Celice, Isaac will finally be liberated, we hear.","322":"(Celice): No, my own strength is nothing at all. It's all thanks to the strength of the people of Isaac.","323":"(Celice): It is I who have been helped, all this long time.","324":"(Elder): Come to think of it, what a strange turn of fate this is. Isaac's former king trusted Lord Sigurd's father,","325":"(Elder): Lord Sigurd helped Prince Shanan, and now Prince Shanan helps you in turn — truly, a trick of destiny.","326":"(Celice): Isaac is like a second homeland to me too. I hope to remain eternal friends with Prince Shanan.","327":"(Elder): That you are the rightful heir to the Grannvale royal family —","328":"(Elder): there is no longer a single person who doubts that.","329":"(Elder): Please, carry the banner of justice onward to Belhalla.","330":"(After capturing Sophara Castle)","331":"(Celice): Nanna, it's dangerous to be out in a place like this.","332":"(Nanna): Ah, yes, I'm fine.","333":"(Celice): But please be careful — you're an easy target, Nanna, so don't go to the front line.","334":"(Nanna): But...","335":"(Celice): Nanna... I'm worried about you.","336":"(Nanna): ...yes, Lord Celice...","337":"(After capturing Sophara Castle)","338":"(Celice): Julia, are you alright?","339":"(Julia): Oh, Lord Celice...","340":"(Celice): I'll give this to you, Julia. I found it in Sophara Castle.","341":"(Julia): What is this...?","342":"(Celice): It's a light tome called Aura, apparently. You should be able to use it, right?","343":"(Julia): Aura... somehow, this name feels nostalgic...","344":"(Julia): Lord Celice, thank you very much.","345":"(After capturing Isaac Castle)","346":"(Celice): Julia, are you alright?","347":"(Julia): Oh, Lord Celice...","348":"(Celice): I'll give this to you, Julia. I found it in Isaac Castle.","349":"(Julia): What is this...?","350":"(Celice): It's a light tome called Resire, apparently. You should be able to use it, right?","351":"(Julia): Yes, if it's a light tome, then...","352":"(Celice): Good. This should be able to protect you.","353":"(Julia): Lord Celice... thank you very much.","354":"(Villager (woman)): Huh? Aren't you Dimna? Yes, you're Dimna, aren't you!","355":"(Dimna): Eh? Karen? It's really you, Karen! It's been so long.","356":"(Villager (woman)): It really has been forever! How many years has it been since you and Mana left this town...","357":"(Villager (woman)): But I'm so glad, you look well.","358":"(Dimna): Yeah, Lord Celice rose up to liberate the world from the Empire's rule, and I joined up with him too.","359":"(Dimna): Though I'm still not much help yet.","360":"(Villager (woman)): Hehe, how dashing. When you were little you used to cry every day because of me...","361":"(Dimna): Hahaha, you promised never to bring that up. But you know, I keep thinking I need to grow even stronger.","362":"(Dimna): So that Karen and everyone in the world can live in peace.","363":"(Villager (woman)): I see... good luck, I'm rooting for you...","364":"(Dimna): What's wrong? Why are you looking down like that?","365":"(Villager (woman)): No, it's nothing... here, take this with you, I'm sure it'll come in handy.","366":"(Dimna): What's this?","367":"(Villager (woman)): It's my mother's keepsake necklace. Wearing it is supposed to give you strength.","368":"(Dimna): Wha, I can't accept something like that!","369":"(Villager (woman)): No, it's fine — if you have it, my mother would be happy too, that the time has come for this necklace's power to be used.","370":"(Villager (woman)): ...please, take it.","371":"(Dimna): ...thank you, I'll hold onto it. But once this war is over, I'll definitely come back to return it.","372":"(Villager (woman)): Heh, that's just like you, Dimna...","373":"(Dimna): Well then, everyone's waiting, so I'll be off now. Karen, take care!","374":"(Villager (woman)): You take care too, Dimna!","375":"(Villager (woman)): Dimna.........","376":"(Slayder): This is King Danan's order — I won't let you go any further than this!","377":"(Slayder): Lord Danan... forgive me!","378":"(Danan): You damned rebels! Don't you dare underestimate the Grannvale Empire!","379":"(Danan): Guh... ...Emperor Arvis...","380":"(Levin (Strategist)): Well done, Celice. The liberation of Isaac has ended safely.","381":"(Celice): Levin, you're back.","382":"(Levin (Strategist)): Yes... I only just returned. Celice, the world is in upheaval right now. Do you know why?","383":"(Celice): Huh? No... I still don't quite...","384":"(Levin (Strategist)): It's been fifteen years since the world was unified under Lord Arvis and the Grannvale Empire was born. At first it wasn't so bad.","385":"(Levin (Strategist)): Emperor Arvis ruled the world with absolute rule of law,","386":"(Levin (Strategist)): and though it was a bit stifling, a peaceful, calm span of time flowed by.","387":"(Levin (Strategist)): But over these past few years, the emperor's ways have changed completely — rule by force, oppression of the people,","388":"(Levin (Strategist)): and... the revival of the heretical faith. The Loptr cult's power now threatens to cover the whole world,","389":"(Levin (Strategist)): sacrificial rites have been revived too, and for the sake of the Loptr god's resurrection festival, children are being hunted down across the world.","390":"(Levin (Strategist)): Those who resist it are all captured and either enslaved or executed,","391":"(Levin (Strategist)): and truly, that detestable Loptr Empire is on the verge of being rebuilt.","392":"(Celice): That can't be...! I'd heard rumors, but... I never imagined it was really true...","393":"(Levin (Strategist)): Isaac still has it better than most. It seems Danan's two sons refused to go along with the child-hunting, at least.","394":"(Celice): .........","395":"(Levin (Strategist)): Right now, uprisings are breaking out all over the world, but none of them have any unity,","396":"(Levin (Strategist)): and they're being crushed before the Empire's overwhelming military might.","397":"(Levin (Strategist)): The world needs a savior right now. Do you understand, Celice? It is you who must save the world.","398":"(Levin (Strategist)): You're the only one who can do it.","399":"(Celice): Please wait. I don't have that kind of power...","400":"(Levin (Strategist)): You have the duty to do it. You are the eldest child of Princess Deirdre, which makes you the elder brother of Prince Julius.","401":"(Levin (Strategist)): As a direct descendant of the saint Heim, you have the duty to unite the holy warriors and save the world from darkness.","402":"(Celice): That's...","403":"(Levin (Strategist)): And besides, you have the power too. It hasn't awakened yet, but you are a descendant of the holy knight Baldur,","404":"(Levin (Strategist)): and if you take up the holy sword Tyrfing, that power should reach to the heavens.","405":"(Celice): But...","406":"(Levin (Strategist)): And finally, there is the will of the gods.","407":"(Levin (Strategist)): As the son of Sigurd, who met such an unjust death, you must carry on his will.","408":"(Levin (Strategist)): This is no longer the time for hesitation. Do you understand, Celice?","409":"(Celice): Yes... I understand... if that is my fate, then I will go. Following the will of the gods...","410":"(Levin (Strategist)): Fate is not just one thing. Nor does it belong only to you. In time, you'll come to understand that too.","411":"(Levin (Strategist)): Sigurd left you with a great many things — and the greatest of them is friendship. The fact that I stand with you now is one of those.","412":"(Levin (Strategist)): Be grateful that so many young people gather around you because of your father's kindness.","413":"(Celice): Yes, my father was loved and trusted by so many people. I hope to be the same way.","414":"(Levin (Strategist)): Then it's settled. Now then, our next destination is Leonster.","415":"(Levin (Strategist)): The son of Quan, Sigurd's close friend, has raised an army at Leonster, but they're struggling. We must go save them.","416":"(Levin (Strategist)): Let's leave Isaac's defense to the people of this country and set out at once.","417":"(Levin (Strategist)): We can rejoin Prince Shanan along the way.","418":"(Celice): Yes!","419":"(Elder): King Danan had three children — the eldest, Bryan, is in Grannvale, but the younger two remained in this country.","420":"(Elder): Johan is Isaac's lord, and Johalva is Sophara's lord,","421":"(Elder): and funnily enough, the two of them are both in love with Lakche of the Liberation Army, and they're forever at each other's throats over it.","422":"(Elder): Well, neither of them is a thoroughly bad person at heart, so maybe we could win them over as allies...","423":"(Villager (man)): We people of Isaac look up to Lord Celice.","424":"(Villager (man)): Your father, Lord Sigurd, once helped Prince Shanan — we will never forget that debt!","425":"(Villager (man)): Prince Shanan is our hope. If only the holy sword Balmung would return to the prince's hand,","426":"(Villager (man)): we'd have nothing to fear from the Empire's men — we'd drive them out of this country, every last one!","427":"(Villager (man)): Oh, so you're the Liberation Army!? You've finally risen up!","428":"(Villager (man)): We did it! Now we can finally drive the Empire's men out of this country!","429":"(Villager (woman)): Lord Celice of the Liberation Army is the rightful heir to Grannvale, isn't he?","430":"(Villager (woman)): Then surely you'll help us too!","431":"(Villager (woman)): As thanks, please accept this skill ring. I hope you'll do your best.","432":"(Villager (woman)): I hear that in other countries, children are being hunted down...","433":"(Villager (woman)): Thanks to all of you, Isaac has been liberated, but the world is still shrouded in darkness...","434":"(Villager (woman)): There are people suffering under the Empire's tyranny who are waiting for Lord Celice's help.","435":"(Villager (woman)): Please, return to Grannvale as soon as you possibly can!"};
